<h2>Basic Terminal Commands</h2>
<p>It's fine if the terminal feels unfamiliar. Our goal reaches only as far as <strong>"create a new folder, go to that location, and run <code>claude</code>"</strong>. The AI does everything after that. On Windows, launching <strong>PowerShell</strong> usually starts you in your user folder.</p>

<h3>Remember just these four</h3>
<div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Command</th><th>Meaning</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>pwd</code></td><td>print working directory</td><td>Shows which folder you are in right now</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>cd &lt;folder&gt;</code></td><td>change directory</td><td>Move to another folder (e.g. <code>cd Downloads</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>mkdir &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>make directory</td><td>Create a new folder (e.g. <code>mkdir kist-test</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>claude</code></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Run Claude Code in the current folder</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

